<Doc slug={slug} title="Install">
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p>cortex needs Go 1.26.2 or newer to build from source. Release archives cover Linux and macOS on amd64 and arm64, plus native Windows on amd64.</p>

  <h2>Build from source</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/atakang7/cortex.git
cd cortex
go build -o cortex ./cmd/cortex
./cortex --version</code></pre>
  <p>In Windows PowerShell, use <code>go build -o cortex.exe ./cmd/cortex</code>. The native Windows build uses Git Bash when available and PowerShell otherwise.</p>

  <h2>Go install</h2>
  <pre><code>go install github.com/atakang7/cortex/v2/cmd/cortex@latest</code></pre>
  <p>Ensure your Go binary directory is on <code>PATH</code>.</p>

  <h2>Release binaries</h2>
  <p>Get the matching archive from <a href="https://github.com/atakang7/cortex/releases">GitHub Releases</a>. Linux and macOS users can run the checked-in installer, which installs to <code>~/.local/bin</code> by default:</p>
  <pre><code>curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atakang7/cortex/main/scripts/install.sh
sh install.sh</code></pre>
  <p>Set <code>CORTEX_INSTALL_DIR</code> to choose a different location. On Windows, use the native source build or the Windows release ZIP.</p>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
